meta {
  name: My Usage
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/auth/usage
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.account_type: isString
  res.body.limited: isBoolean
  res.body.free_limits: isDefined
  res.body.trees: isArray
}

docs {
  # My Usage

  The caller's own trees — people and marriages in each — against the quotas of their plan. `account_type` is the plan in force today: a paid plan whose `paid_until` day has passed already reads `free`, before the daily expiry task stores it. `days_left` counts today, and is null when the plan never lapses or is free. `free_limits` always carries the free quotas, so a client can show them to a paid account too.

  ## Output `200`
  ```json
  {
    "account_type": "free",
    "paid_until": null,
    "days_left": null,
    "limited": true,
    "free_limits": { "owned_trees": 2, "persons_per_tree": 20, "marriages_per_tree": 8 },
    "owned_trees": 1,
    "trees": [
      { "tree_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000010", "name": "Family", "persons": 14, "marriages": 3 }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Requires `Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}` (run Login first).
}
